    ("Jo tuonne ma sinun manoan", "Jo tuonne minä sinun manaan", "jo, tuonne, minä, sinä, manata", "already, there, I, you, to banish", "Now there I banish you", "The final destination of banishment — Rutja's fierce rapids where trees fall headfirst — recycles, almost verbatim, the same description Lemminkäinen used in Runo 6 for the place he would magically banish the Lapp wizards. This is the third or fourth recurrence of nearly identical incantation formulae across different speakers, suggesting these are traditional, reusable magical 'spell templates' within the oral epic tradition — a key insight into how trickster-style verbal magic functions structurally in the Kalevala."),
